<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">King Wu of Zhou</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1043 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> · Also known as Ji Fa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">King Wu was the founding king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhou-dynasty">Zhou dynasty</a>. Continuing the work of his father King Wen, he led the Zhou and their allies against the Shang and defeated its last king, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/di-xin">Di Xin</a>, at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-muye">Battle of Muye</a>, traditionally dated 1046 BCE. He granted fiefs to relatives, allies and descendants of earlier ruling houses, among them the lords of Qi, Chen and Cai. He died soon after the conquest, leaving his brother the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-zhou">Duke of Zhou</a> as regent.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/king-wu-of-zhou.jpg" alt="King Wu of Zhou" width="320" height="706" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ma Lin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Wu_of_Zhou.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
